@startuml proposed-gateway-trust-boundary
!theme plain
autonumber
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 11

title API GATEWAY - CURRENT TRUST BOUNDARY BEHAVIOUR

actor Client
participant "GatewayTrustBoundaryFilter" as Filter
participant "Gateway route chain" as Chain
participant "Downstream service" as Service

Client -> Filter : request(path, headers)

alt any path segment equals "internal" (case-insensitive)
  Filter --> Client : 403 Forbidden
else public path
  Filter -> Filter : generate a new UUID requestId
  Filter -> Filter : remove exact RESERVED headers\nand prefixes x-verified-, x-internal-, x-authenticated-
  Filter -> Filter : set X-Request-Id to new UUID
  Filter -> Chain : sanitized request
  Chain -> Service : routed request
  Service --> Chain : response
  Chain --> Filter : response
  Filter --> Client : response + X-Request-Id
end

note right of Filter #FFF2CC
  Current code does NOT remove arbitrary x-actor-* headers.
  Downstream services must continue to ignore them, or Gateway
  should add x-actor-* to the blocked prefixes.
end note

@enduml
